            <div xml:id="d704">

                <pb facs="0919" n="908" sameAs="frus:frus1937v02/pg908"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">867N.01/902: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul at Geneva</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Buchnell</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Geneva</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1937-09-16T23:00:00+01:00">September 16, 1937—11
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received September 16—5:35 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>305. Consulate’s 294, September 14, 8 p.m.<anchor n="39" xml:id="d704-f1"/> The
                    Council this afternoon passed a resolution<anchor n="40" xml:id="d704-f2"/>
                    authorizing the British Government to proceed with a study of the British
                    proposal for the partition of Palestine, it being understood that the British
                    Government would submit a report to the Council and that the Council reserved
                    its position on the substance of the question. Text of resolution will be
                    mailed.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Bucknell</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
